 "_comment": "The daily round (movement M4). `workplaces` maps an occupation to candidate nav places (the sim binds the nearest to home). `archetypes` are the office-pegged leg templates; `occupations` assigns each of the 65 trades one. `routes` overrides the ~20 authored majors by 5-char id. A leg's `at` is `home`, `workplace`, or a nav place display name / site id; `doing` is work|trade|sleep|pray|idle|draw_water|stand; `from` is the office the leg begins at; `only_on` restricts it to weekdays (market days move the crowd). `curfew_exempt` keeps night trades in the street at the Snuffing. The two market-trader archetypes split the crowd across the four market squares (lore/core_lore/trade_and_daily_life.md: Highmarket chiefly at the Wickmarket AND Coswald's Yard, Lowmarket at the Tallage AND Maren's Green): `market_trader` works the Wickmarket/Tallage pair (the weighed and chartered goods — candles, bread, cloth, salt, spice, provisions), `market_trader_green` the Coswald's Yard/Maren's Green pair (the raw provisions and open stalls — fish off the moorings, meat out of the Shambles, the general sellers). The split keeps every trade based at the Wickmarket or the Tallage on its own square's pair, so a market day always raises a square above its ordinary working crowd instead of draining it. Bellday closes the generic trades and fills the nave (04_the_round.md §5): the day_worker and market-trader templates lie in at the Kindling and pray at The Lanthorn from Dayspring through the Waning; the wharf trades keep their before-dawn work but join the nave at Dayspring (Wyn Alder's canon route). The night trades (tavern, watch, lamplighter), the clerics (already at prayer) and the anchoress are the exceptions. The day_worker and wharf templates take dinner at home at High Wick (`from: high_wick, at: home` — food & items M2, `features/food_and_items/03_hunger.md` §4): the hearth feeds those legs, so the city's hunger collapses at noon where the player is watching. The market traders stay at their stalls through noon (the market's peak) and eat at supper instead — the vendors M3 binds to the stalls.",

